{
  "profile": "UK adult public-chat moderation regex families",
  "notes": [
    "Build input only: these patterns are copied into chat-filter.regex-patterns alongside the separately curated literal list.",
    "For MineplayPunishments ChatFilter: RE2/J case-insensitive find after NFKC normalization and removal of Unicode FORMAT characters. Do not copy into a different engine without checking semantics.",
    "ASCII spaces, dots, underscores and hyphens between letters, plus selected conventional digit substitutions, are supported. Not every possible evasion or repeated-letter form is covered.",
    "Ambiguous UK vocabulary is intentionally limited to whole-message directed insults. These rules do not identify intent, quotations, irony or all contexts; moderators still review reports.",
    "Standalone threat, solicitation, self-harm and praise rules intentionally allow longer sentences so negated advice, reporting and Minecraft instructions are not indiscriminately blocked. This also leaves evasions for human moderation.",
    "Examples under allowed describe this rule and are intended to remain allowed by the assembled preset unless the final literal policy explicitly documents otherwise.",
    "Basic swearing such as fuck, shit, bloody, arse and bollocks is intentionally outside this preset. Identity, nationality, religion, orientation, 88 and 1488 are not blanket rules."
